IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Employment Claims Act 2016 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation in force from 1/4/2025.
-- THE NOUNS MODULE: the types every other module of this encoding uses, and nothing else (no rules, no #EVAL).
-- Target compiler: main (build 109).  Source: ECA2016.txt, a converter script's plain-text rendering of Singapore Statutes Online, not the official text.
-- A noun is a thing a witness of ordinary competence could testify to; whether it makes anything lawful or unlawful is a rule, and lives in the module of the section that says so.

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- The three families of dispute (s 2(1)), and the matters the Schedules list.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- The First Schedule, "Specified contractual dispute matters": 18 items, named in the Act's words.
-- The item number is given by `sch 1 item number of` in eca-schedules.
DECLARE `First Schedule matter` IS ONE OF
    `Allowance (however described in the contract of service)`
    `Annual wage supplement`
    `Bonus payment`
    `Commission`
    `Deduction from salary`
    `Employment assistance payment`
    `Incentive payment (however described in the contract of service)`
    `Medical benefit`
    `Overtime payment`
    `Pay for extra work`
    `Pay for public holiday or paid leave`
    `Pay for work on public holiday`
    `Pay for work on rest day`
    `Payment in lieu of unconsumed leave`
    `Reimbursement for expenses incurred while carrying out official duties`
    `Salary`
    `Salary in lieu of notice of termination`
    `Termination benefit (including retrenchment benefit or retirement benefit)`

-- The Second Schedule, "Specified statutory dispute matters": 47 items (1 to 45, with 4A and 10A), each named by its item number and a short gloss of the Act's words.
-- The full item is quoted beside its row in eca-schedules.
DECLARE `Second Schedule matter` IS ONE OF
    `Item 1: female employee's paid maternity leave, and payment for working in the benefit period before confinement (CDCA 2001 s 9)`
    `Item 2: female employee's paid adoption leave (CDCA 2001 s 12AA)`
    `Item 3: employee's paid childcare leave (CDCA 2001 s 12B(1) and (9))`
    `Item 4: employee's paid extended childcare leave (CDCA 2001 s 12B(1A) and (9))`
    `Item 4A: employee's paid shared parental leave (CDCA 2001 s 12DA)`
    `Item 5: male employee's paid shared parental leave (CDCA 2001 s 12E)`
    `Item 6: male employee's paid paternity leave (CDCA 2001 s 12H)`
    `Item 7: female part-time employee's paid maternity leave (CDCA Part-Time Employees Regs 2008 reg 4)`
    `Item 8: part-time employee's paid childcare leave (CDCA Part-Time Employees Regs 2008 reg 5)`
    `Item 9: part-time employee's paid extended childcare leave (CDCA Part-Time Employees Regs 2008 reg 5A)`
    `Item 10: female part-time employee's paid adoption leave (CDCA Part-Time Employees Regs 2008 reg 7)`
    `Item 10A: part-time employee's paid shared parental leave (CDCA Part-Time Employees Regs 2008 reg 7A)`
    `Item 11: male part-time employee's paid shared parental leave (CDCA Part-Time Employees Regs 2008 reg 8)`
    `Item 12: male part-time employee's paid paternity leave (CDCA Part-Time Employees Regs 2008 reg 9)`
    `Item 13: employee's payment where the employer ends the contract of service without notice (EA 1968 s 11(1))`
    `Item 14: employer's payment where the employee ends the contract of service without notice (EA 1968 s 11(1))`
    `Item 15: employee's payment where the employer breaks the contract of service (EA 1968 s 16)`
    `Item 16: employer's payment where the employee breaks the contract of service (EA 1968 s 16)`
    `Item 17: employee's payment of salary (EA 1968 s 21, 22 or 23)`
    `Item 18: employee's recovery of a deduction from salary prohibited by EA 1968 s 26`
    `Item 19: employee's payment for working on a rest day at the employee's own request (EA 1968 s 37(2))`
    `Item 20: employee's payment for working on a rest day at the employer's request (EA 1968 s 37(3))`
    `Item 21: employee's overtime pay for extra work at the employer's request (EA 1968 s 38(4))`
    `Item 22: payment for extra work, for an employee to whom EA 1968 s 40 applies (EA 1968 s 40(4))`
    `Item 23: employee's paid annual leave (EA 1968 s 88A)`
    `Item 24: workman's recovery of salary not paid in legal tender (EA 1968 s 57, subject to s 63)`
    `Item 25: workman's recovery of salary from a principal, contractor or subcontractor (EA 1968 s 65)`
    `Item 26: female employee's paid maternity leave, and payment for working in the benefit period before confinement (EA 1968 s 76)`
    `Item 27: payment to the person nominated by, or the personal representative of, a female employee on her death (EA 1968 s 79 and s 80(4))`
    `Item 28: employee's paid childcare leave (EA 1968 s 87A)`
    `Item 29: employee's paid holiday on a public holiday (EA 1968 s 88(1))`
    `Item 30: extra day's salary if required to work on a public holiday (EA 1968 s 88(4))`
    `Item 31: extra day's salary or time off in lieu if required to work on a public holiday (EA 1968 s 88(4A))`
    `Item 32: employee's paid sick leave, and medical examination fees borne by the employer (EA 1968 s 89)`
    `Item 33: part-time employee's payment for working on a rest day at the employee's own request (EA Part-Time Employees Regs reg 4(1))`
    `Item 34: part-time employee's payment for working on a rest day at the employer's request (EA Part-Time Employees Regs reg 4(2))`
    `Item 35: part-time employee's overtime pay (EA Part-Time Employees Regs reg 5(1))`
    `Item 36: part-time employee's paid holiday on a public holiday (EA Part-Time Employees Regs reg 6(1))`
    `Item 37: part-time employee's sum for one day's work if required to work on a public holiday (EA Part-Time Employees Regs reg 6(2))`
    `Item 38: part-time employee's sum or time off in lieu if required to work on a public holiday (EA Part-Time Employees Regs reg 6(2A))`
    `Item 39: part-time employee's allowance for relinquishing paid holidays (EA Part-Time Employees Regs reg 6(4))`
    `Item 40: part-time employee's paid annual leave (EA Part-Time Employees Regs reg 7(1) and (2))`
    `Item 41: part-time employee's allowance for relinquishing paid annual leave (EA Part-Time Employees Regs reg 7(3))`
    `Item 42: part-time employee's paid sick leave (EA Part-Time Employees Regs reg 8)`
    `Item 43: part-time employee's paid childcare leave (EA Part-Time Employees Regs reg 8A)`
    `Item 44: female part-time employee's paid maternity leave (EA Part-Time Employees Regs reg 9)`
    `Item 45: employee's employment assistance payment (RRA 1993 s 7C(1))`

-- The Third Schedule, "Wrongful dismissal disputes": 3 items.
DECLARE `Third Schedule matter` IS ONE OF
    `Item 1: dismissal without just cause or excuse, where the employee may claim under EA 1968 s 14(2)`
    `Item 2: notice of dismissal to a female employee without sufficient cause, where she may claim under EA 1968 s 84(2)`
    `Item 3: notice of dismissal without sufficient cause to a female employee mentioned in CDCA 2001 s 12(1), who may claim under EA 1968 s 84(2) as applied`

-- The Fourth Schedule, "Specified obligations under written law": 3 items.
DECLARE `Fourth Schedule obligation` IS ONE OF
    `Item 1: an employer's obligations under EA 1968 s 95, 95A and 96`
    `Item 2: an employer's obligations under para 6A of Part IV of the Fourth Schedule to the Employment of Foreign Manpower (Work Passes) Regulations 2012`
    `Item 3: an employer's obligations under para 5 of Part II of the Fifth Schedule to the Employment of Foreign Manpower (Work Passes) Regulations 2012`

-- What a dispute is about: one of the three families of s 2(1), or none of the matters the Schedules list.
DECLARE `Matter of a dispute` IS ONE OF
    `A matter in the First Schedule` HAS item IS A `First Schedule matter`
    `A matter in the Second Schedule` HAS item IS A `Second Schedule matter`
    `A matter in the Third Schedule` HAS item IS A `Third Schedule matter`
    `None of the matters in the Schedules`

-- A dispute, as a witness could describe it (s 2(1) "specified contractual dispute", "specified statutory dispute", "wrongful dismissal dispute").
DECLARE Dispute HAS
    matter IS A `Matter of a dispute`
    `relates to a payment of an amount of money` IS A BOOLEAN
    `arises out of or in the course of employment under a contract of service` IS A BOOLEAN
    `relates to the dismissal of an employee` IS A BOOLEAN

-- The kinds of approval that make an individual an approved mediator (s 2(1) "approved mediator" (a) to (e)).
DECLARE `Approval for mediation` IS ONE OF
    `A mediation under Part 2 of a specified employment dispute`
    `A tripartite mediation`
    `A mediation mentioned in section 115(2A) of the Employment Act 1968`
    `A consultation or conciliation under section 8A(5) of the Retirement and Re-employment Act 1993`
    `A mediation or conciliation under another written law relating to employment that the Commissioner has determined`

-- s 2(1) "claim": a claim, or a counterclaim.
DECLARE `Kind of claim` IS ONE OF
    `A claim`
    `A counterclaim`

-- s 2(1) "claim referral certificate" (a) and (b): the provision a certificate was issued under.
DECLARE `Provision a certificate was issued under` IS ONE OF
    `Section 6(2) of the Employment Claims Act 2016`
    `Section 7(7)(a) of the Employment Claims Act 2016`
    `Section 30H(6) of the Industrial Relations Act 1960`
    `Some other provision`

-- s 2(1) "Registrar".
DECLARE `Office for the tribunals` IS ONE OF
    `The registrar`
    `A deputy registrar`
    `An assistant registrar`
    `Another officer`

-- s 2(1) "tribunal magistrate".
DECLARE `How a tribunal magistrate came to be one` IS ONE OF
    `Appointed under section 9(1)(a)`
    `Designated under section 9(5)`
    `Neither`

-- s 2(2): the two roles the Act's words "claimant" and "respondent" name, and a person who may fill them.
DECLARE `Role named in the Act` IS ONE OF
    `The claimant`
    `The respondent`

DECLARE Person HAS
    name IS A STRING

-- s 2(3): the officers of the Labour Commissioner's office.
DECLARE `Labour officer` IS ONE OF
    `A Deputy Commissioner for Labour`
    `A Principal Assistant Commissioner for Labour`
    `An Assistant Commissioner for Labour`
    `Another officer`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Part 2: mediation (ss 3 to 7).
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- s 3(2) (a) to (g): which paragraph's time limit a dispute falls under.  (f) and (g) are decided by whether the employment relationship has ended.
DECLARE `Kind of dispute for the time limit` IS ONE OF
    `Recovery of salary under section 65 of the Employment Act 1968`
    `Re-employment dispute described in section 8A(3) of the Retirement and Re-employment Act 1993`
    `Re-employment dispute under section 8B(7) of the Retirement and Re-employment Act 1993`
    `Wrongful dismissal dispute for a claim mentioned in section 14(2) of the Employment Act 1968`
    `Wrongful dismissal dispute for a claim mentioned in section 84(2) of the Employment Act 1968`
    `Another specified employment dispute`

-- The dates s 3(2) counts from.  A date the dispute does not need, or the person cannot give, is NOTHING.
DECLARE `Facts for the mediation request time limit` HAS
    kind IS A `Kind of dispute for the time limit`
    `the employment relationship has ended` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the last day of the period in section 65(2A) of the Employment Act 1968, as extended under section 65(2B)` IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the last day of employment of the employee` IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the last day of the time determined under section 8B(8) of the Retirement and Re-employment Act 1993` IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the date of the dismissal of the employee` IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the date of the employee's confinement` IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the date on which the material facts giving rise to the earliest specified employment dispute listed in the mediation request occurred` IS A MAYBE DATE

-- Who does what under the Act, for the regulative rules (PARTY ... MUST / SHANT).
DECLARE `Actor under the Act` IS ONE OF
    Claimant
    Respondent
    Commissioner
    `Approved mediator`
    `Tribunal`
    `A party`

DECLARE `Act under the Act` IS ONE OF
    `submit a mediation request`
    `refer every listed specified employment dispute for mediation`
    `conduct the first mediation session`
    `issue a claim referral certificate`
    `be represented by an advocate and solicitor`
    `be represented by an agent`
    `disclose to every party the evidence and information the tribunal obtained itself`
    `make a summary of the facts and issues in dispute, and notes of the proceedings`

-- s 5(2): who a party is, and who the party's representative is.
DECLARE `Kind of party` IS ONE OF
    `An individual`
    `The Government`
    `A body corporate`
    `A partnership`
    `An unincorporated association`

DECLARE `Kind of representative` IS ONE OF
    `An advocate and solicitor`
    `An agent, whether paid or otherwise`
    `A public officer`
    `An officer of the body corporate`
    `A full-time employee of the party`
    `A partner of the partnership`
    `A member of the governing body of the unincorporated association`
    `Another individual prescribed by regulations`
    `Anyone else`

-- s 5(5) "officer" of a body corporate.
DECLARE `Position in a body corporate` IS ONE OF
    `Director`
    `Partner`
    `Member of the committee of management`
    `Chief executive`
    `Manager`
    `Secretary`
    `Another position`

-- s 7(5)(b)(ii): which kind of mediation a District Court refers a dispute to.
DECLARE `Where a settlement agreement arose` IS ONE OF
    `From a mediation under Part 2`
    `From a tripartite mediation conducted by an approved mediator`

DECLARE `Kind of mediation referred to` IS ONE OF
    `Mediation under Part 2`
    `Tripartite mediation to be conducted by an approved mediator`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Part 3: employment claims (ss 8 to 27).
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- s 12(2): who makes the claim, and against whom.
DECLARE `Who makes the claim` IS ONE OF
    `The employee`
    `A person entitled under a written law to receive the amount claimed in place of the employee`
    `The employer`
    `A person entitled under a written law to receive the amount claimed in place of the employer`
    `Someone else making the claim`

DECLARE `Whom the claim is made against` IS ONE OF
    `The employer of the employee`
    `A person liable under section 65 of the Employment Act 1968 for the employee's salary`
    `An employee of the employer`
    `Someone else the claim is made against`

-- s 16(3) to (8): the representations in writing to a Minister that bar or end a claim.
DECLARE `Representations to a Minister` IS ONE OF
    `Representations in writing under section 35(3) of the Industrial Relations Act 1960`
    `Representations in writing under section 8(1) of the Retirement and Re-employment Act 1993`
    `Representations in writing under section 8B(1) of the Retirement and Re-employment Act 1993`
    `No such representations`

-- ss 17, 23, 24, 25: courts the Act names.
DECLARE `Court named in the Act` IS ONE OF
    `The General Division of the High Court`
    `A District Court`
    `A Magistrate's Court`
    `Another court`

-- s 21(2): an obligation of a party under a written law.
DECLARE `Obligation of a party under a written law` IS ONE OF
    `A Fourth Schedule obligation` HAS item IS A `Fourth Schedule obligation`
    `Some other obligation`

-- s 22(1): the orders a tribunal may make.
DECLARE `Order of a tribunal` IS ONE OF
    `An order requiring a party to pay money to another party`
    `An order dismissing the whole or any part of the claim`
    `An order requiring a party to pay costs to another party`
    `An order requiring an employer to reinstate an employee in the employee's former employment`
    `Another kind of order`

-- s 22(8): where the claim arose.
DECLARE `Where a claim arose` IS ONE OF
    `From a mediation under Part 2 of a specified employment dispute`
    `From a tripartite mediation conducted by an approved mediator`
    `From neither of those`

-- s 23(1): the grounds of an appeal.
DECLARE `Ground of appeal` IS ONE OF
    `A ground involving a question of law`
    `That the claim was outside the jurisdiction of the tribunal`
    `A question of fact`
    `Another ground`

-- s 23(4): the orders of a District Court that are final.
DECLARE `Order of a District Court on an appeal` IS ONE OF
    `An order giving or refusing permission under section 23(2)`
    `An order extending or refusing to extend under section 23(3)(a) the time under section 22(10)`
    `An order remitting or refusing to remit under section 23(3)(b) a matter to a tribunal`
    `Another order`

-- s 25(1) and (2): what the General Division of the High Court may do on an appeal.
DECLARE `Step on appeal` IS ONE OF
    `Dismiss the appeal`
    `Allow the appeal and set aside or vary the order`
    `Remit the matter to the tribunal for reconsideration, or order a rehearing by a different tribunal`
    `Make any other order, including an order as to costs and expenses`
    `Reverse or vary a determination made by a tribunal on a question of fact`
    `Receive further evidence`
    `Some other step`

-- s 26: what the General Division of the High Court's decision is on.
DECLARE `Matter decided by the General Division of the High Court` IS ONE OF
    `An appeal against an order made by a tribunal`
    `An application for a stay of execution or enforcement of an order made by a tribunal`
    `Another matter`

-- s 27(1): an allegation.
DECLARE `Allegation about a duty or a relationship` IS ONE OF
    `That the person is not the employer or employee of the claimant`
    `That the person is not a person who has a duty under the Child Development Co-Savings Act 2001, the Employment Act 1968 or the Retirement and Re-employment Act 1993`
    `Another allegation`

-- Part 4 (ss 28 to 35).
DECLARE `What a provision of an agreement purports to do` IS ONE OF
    `Exclude or limit the jurisdiction of a tribunal`
    `Prevent a person from submitting a mediation request`
    `Prevent a person from making a claim, an application or an appeal under this Act`
    `Something else`

DECLARE `Person who may disclose under section 29` IS ONE OF
    `The Commissioner`
    `An approved mediator`
    `A tribunal magistrate`
    `A Registrar`
    `Someone else who holds information`

DECLARE `Person protected under section 30(3)` IS ONE OF
    `The Commissioner`
    `An individual authorised to carry out a function or duty of the Commissioner under this Act`
    `An approved mediator`
    `Someone else`

DECLARE `Actor in the proceedings` IS ONE OF
    `The tribunal`
    `The claimant in the proceedings`
    `The respondent in the proceedings`
    `A District Court`
    `The General Division of the High Court`

DECLARE `Act in the proceedings` IS ONE OF
    `disclose to every party the evidence and information obtained under section 21(5)`
    `make a summary of the facts and issues in dispute, as determined by the tribunal`
    `make notes of the proceedings`
    `correct an order made by the tribunal`
    `identify the relevant issues in the claim`
    `ensure that the relevant evidence is adduced by the parties`
